                                        "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                        "entry_id": "5321b282-cee7-3ad2-bec3-536bcd167cb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The reflexive form of they, the third-person singular personal pronoun. The single person previously mentioned, as the object of a verb or following a preposition (also used for emphasis)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pronoun",
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "reflexive",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "third-person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2123387f-70f3-4ded-a478-9ac54c1ff9f9",
                                                "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                                "text": "Someone could hurt themself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fa0ad7f-bcfa-483b-805f-81abab796258",
                                                "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                                "text": "Anyone who wants a car like mine can buy one themself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "002daf0a-b738-465f-bd75-4e57414782d8",
                                                "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                                "text": "[…] they woulden't ^([sic]) always be trying to make Themself Look Diffarunt ^([sic]) from what nature made Them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "062d89ff-b412-4177-973f-3c7879708175",
                                                "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                                "text": "THE author who masqueraded as Helen Demidenko yesterday urged the hoaxer who deceived the respected right-wing journal Quadrant to unmask themself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0111dc12-b371-4885-8a3b-7f0e395b37b9",
                                                "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                                "text": "... somedays there will be an odd number of quadders and so somebody might have to sit by themself in the back."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "785e2223-d39d-4dd8-97c1-eaabdd79c9e9",
                                                "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                                "text": "Someone set themself on fire Friday at the plaza in front of the US Supreme Court building, a court spokesperson said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "487e1e45-dae2-4cbe-b6dd-c496d9007504",
                                                "sense_id": "686390f0-2a2a-3f80-bf7d-8a9ae79d4451",
                                                "text": "Sometimes in modern usage They_(sg) has the reflexive form themself, as in Sometimes a person can surprise themself. (Microsoft Word’s grammar-checking tool doesn’t like this, and peremptorily changes it to themselves – what a nerve!)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "380cf67a-e419-3ec9-9505-aaeb0e1bf156",
                                        "entry_id": "5321b282-cee7-3ad2-bec3-536bcd167cb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of themselves (the third-person plural)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonstandard",
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "third-person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91909981-0abb-4e9f-b345-010484c5b39b",
                                                "sense_id": "380cf67a-e419-3ec9-9505-aaeb0e1bf156",
                                                "text": "[…] and the same is here thought of al men to be so vailable and sufficient, as can be required, accept and take the said commission and dispensation so thankfully, and themself so satisfied with the same, that they repute and think themself not only singularly obstringed and bound to the Popes […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cda20e89-1b84-424d-ba2d-244fe2b5bf7b",
                        "source_entry_id": "158f571d-fd6e-3074-ab3a-0eeba1597ff1",
                        "source_sense_id": "5118e1aa-799c-35c4-8330-d889ec570316",
                        "target_lang_word": "themselves",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "themselves",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29db788a-2854-3949-9732-ca316c787d39",
                                        "entry_id": "e2a22678-4d99-3c32-862f-74aaf6f34c6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The reflexive case of they, the third-person plural personal pronoun. The group of people, animals, or objects previously mentioned, as the object of a verb or following a preposition (also used for emphasis)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pronoun",
                                            "reflexive",
                                            "third-person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8b691ea-a33e-4c2f-aaec-3ee4a3f70731",
                                                "sense_id": "29db788a-2854-3949-9732-ca316c787d39",
                                                "text": "They’ve hurt themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68d674d7-8687-4b22-910f-61cbcfc07c28",
                                                "sense_id": "29db788a-2854-3949-9732-ca316c787d39",
                                                "text": "They fought among themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "631768c6-c313-41af-ae74-fb5f00834da8",
                                                "sense_id": "29db788a-2854-3949-9732-ca316c787d39",
                                                "text": "They are going to try climbing Mount Everest themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6244fbfb-6d74-430d-9761-7210e7d9e017",
                                                "sense_id": "29db788a-2854-3949-9732-ca316c787d39",
                                                "text": "The preposterous altruism too![…]Resist not evil. It is an insane immolation of self—as bad intrinsically as fakirs stabbing themselves or anchorites warping their spines in caves scarcely large enough for a fair-sized dog."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a19096f0-0549-4455-94e2-4cd4e5f94162",
                                                "sense_id": "29db788a-2854-3949-9732-ca316c787d39",
                                                "text": "The real drama came as these two camps fought for undecideds, who literally found themselves in the middle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5516b038-ed3d-3a9a-b92c-7f0ea0e6cf6e",
                                        "entry_id": "e2a22678-4d99-3c32-862f-74aaf6f34c6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The reflexive case of they, the third-person singular personal pronoun. The single person previously mentioned, as the object of a verb or following a preposition (also used for emphasis)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pronoun",
                                            "reflexive",
                                            "third-person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b033e49-b2d1-404c-a1ae-4f40953d55df",
                                                "sense_id": "5516b038-ed3d-3a9a-b92c-7f0ea0e6cf6e",
                                                "text": "Would whoever stole my phone please make themselves known."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63edd58e-b0fe-4f74-bfda-07e357ed0286",
                                                "sense_id": "5516b038-ed3d-3a9a-b92c-7f0ea0e6cf6e",
                                                "text": "I don't want anyone to fight among themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3b62efb-f2c7-4121-8588-a6213e998254",
                                                "sense_id": "5516b038-ed3d-3a9a-b92c-7f0ea0e6cf6e",
                                                "text": "Everyone must do it themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2233d0cd-19fb-4389-a508-b8747ba21388",
                                                "sense_id": "5516b038-ed3d-3a9a-b92c-7f0ea0e6cf6e",
                                                "text": "Let nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8830122-13f5-4b4c-918c-fd2605a30579",
                                                "sense_id": "5516b038-ed3d-3a9a-b92c-7f0ea0e6cf6e",
                                                "text": "In fact she was so busy doing all the things that anyone might, who finds themselves alone in an empty house, that she did not notice at first when it began to turn dusk and the rooms to grow dim."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f87e7219-bc06-49ca-a3fb-c53e968d9b01",
                                                "sense_id": "5516b038-ed3d-3a9a-b92c-7f0ea0e6cf6e",
                                                "text": "“Anyone who has experienced or witnessed an anaphylaxis reaction knows it can be very stressful deciding when to inject epinephrine to themselves or a child and often delay,” Dr. Jonathan Spergel, chief of the allergy program at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia, said in a news release from ARS Pharmaceuticals."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
